{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l223q4dr","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"physics","chapter":"rotational-motion","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"angular-momentum","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pa-thin-uniform-rod-pivoted-at-o-is-rotating-in-the-hori-jee-advanced-physics-units-and-measurements-tqmsdowdj1todtxo","content":"<p>A thin uniform rod, pivoted at O, is rotating in the horizontal plane with constant angular speed <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, as shown in the figure. At time t = 0, a small insect starts from O and moves with constant speed v, with respect to the rod towards the other end. It reaches the end of the rod at t = T and stops. The angular speed of the system remains <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.407ex\" height=\"1.027ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -443 622 454\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> throughout. The magnitude of the torque (|<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.029ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.17ex\" height=\"1.005ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 517 444\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>|) about O, as a function of time is best represented by which plot ?</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Physics - Rotational Motion Question 38 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l24kne3x/e5d77f44-bf61-472e-8e4c-19c524999bca/f067cdd0-bf01-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24kne3y.png?format=png 2500w\"